# Semantic versions

After any change that ships in this repo, bump versions in the **same turn** before finishing. Do not leave the previous version on **changed** crates.

## Which crates

Bump **only crates whose own sources, manifest, or crate-specific docs changed** in this unit of work. Do **not** bump a crate because a sibling moved, because the app moved, or because you raised `[workspace.package].version`.

`[workspace.package].version` in the root `Cargo.toml` is the **app** version. `ft-app` keeps `version.workspace = true`.

Any other crate (`ft-exec`, `ft-store`, `ft-mdns`, …) may use `version.workspace = true` **only if that crate is also bumping in this same unit of work**. If it did not change, it **must** pin `version = "x.y.z"` (drop `version.workspace = true`) at the version it already published. Leaving `version.workspace = true` on an unchanged crate silently gives it the new app version — that is always wrong.

When a previously pinned crate changes later, bump **that crate’s** `version =`, and bump the **app** whenever `ft-app` still consumes the change.

Run a cargo command afterward so `Cargo.lock` matches. `scripts/install-app.sh` reads the `ft-app` version into `Info.plist` — do not hardcode it there.

## Which number

Use [semver](https://semver.org): `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`. Apply the tier to **each bumped crate independently** (a docs-only app fix is a PATCH on `ft-app` even if a library stayed at an older MINOR).

- **PATCH** (`1.0.0` → `1.0.1`): bug fixes, styling, docs, cleanup, no new capability
- **MINOR** (`1.0.1` → `1.1.0`): new backward-compatible behavior or UI
- **MAJOR** (`1.1.0` → `2.0.0`): breaking behavior, removed features, incompatible data/store changes

Bump once per unit of work per crate (the highest tier that applies to that crate). The sidebar brand and crate hover list come from each crate’s `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`.
